# VoiceVision Feature: Custom Hotword File (T028)
# Source: src/voicevision/core/hotwords.py, src/voicevision/listen.py

## HotwordConfig
- words: list[str] - multiple wake words
- threshold: float (0.0-1.0) - reserved for future ML detection

## load_hotwords()
- Priority: explicit path > VOICEVISION_HOTWORDS env > ~/.voicevision/hotwords.json > default
- JSON format: {"words": ["Olá Ambrósio", "Hey Ambrósio"], "threshold": 0.5}
- Default: ["Olá Ambrósio"] with threshold 0.5

## wake_words_detected()
- Case-insensitive, accent-insensitive (NFD normalization)
- Returns (bool, matched_word) - first match wins
- Used by _run_wake_word, _run_wake_word_continuous, _transcribe_utterances

## CLI Integration
- --hotwords-file PATH overrides VOICEVISION_HOTWORDS
- --wake-word "word" replaces first word in list
- Legacy VOICEVISION_WAKE_WORD still works (replaces first word)

## JSON Output
- wake_word_detected: true/false
- wake_word: first configured word (for backward compat)

## History
- Records matched wake word per entry